    fix(aug-208): judge/tier1 launch path supplies DUCKBRAIN_URL so host verdicts grade the real battery
    
    Every gitreins tier-1 verdict recorded on this host (7/7 in
    .gitreins/history/2026-11-23) landed tier1 tests passed=false / exit_code 2
    because the tracked launch path (test_command) ran `bash tests/gate.sh` with no
    DUCKBRAIN_URL, and the gate refuses to self-default: require_live_prerequisites
    aborts with exit 2 at the preflight before pytest ever runs. Environmental red
    on every verdict, tier-2 items PASSing underneath.
    
    Fix: test_command now supplies the local DuckBrain,
    `DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000 bash tests/gate.sh`, with a comment
    explaining the dev-host supply and why the gate must not self-default
    (tests/gate.sh itself is NOT weakened — AC4 fail-closed kept).
    
    Measured (this host, pre-fix):
    
    AC1 (GATE_MODE_ONLY=1):  "gate mode: live", rc=0
    AC4 arm 1 (env -u DUCKBRAIN_URL):
      ERROR: DuckBrain URL missing — set DUCKBRAIN_URL before running the live gate (or use AUGER_CI=1 on hosted CI).   rc=2
    AC4 arm 2 (AUGER_CI=1):
      ERROR: refusing AUGER_CI=1 downgrade on a non-runner host; require GITHUB_ACTIONS=true or CI=1/true.               rc=2
    AC2: tier1 tests exit_code = 2 in 589dd5f9, 8a7e18a2, 36569fbe
      while their tier2 items all read PASS (3 / 7 / 8 items).
    AC5 baseline audit: bound_failed_verdict=27 (unchanged, as expected — the drop
      accumulates as post-fix verdicts re-record).
    
    Launch-path proof: running the exact new test_command string under `timeout 90`
    shows the gate passing the prerequisite preflight and entering the pytest arm
    (progress dots) — first run also crossed py_compile, ruff and the wrapper
    regression before the kill. (Kill expected and fine; the setsid'd pytest
    survivor was reaped by hand after the probe.)
    
    Worktree note: the worktree ships no .venv, so the gate initially fell back to
    an interpreter without dev deps and skipped the pytest arm; .venv was
    provisioned with `uv venv .venv && uv pip install -e '.[dev]'` so the probe
    proves the pytest arm, not a skip. No tracked file touched by that.
    
    Addresses AUG-208.
