   # tests/gate.sh is the repo's whole gate: py_compile + ruff + the end-to-end
   # smoke loop (15 assertions against a live throwaway DuckBrain namespace).
   # Naming the wrapper rather than smoke.sh alone keeps the arms together.
-  test_command: bash tests/gate.sh
+  # AUG-208: test_command is the judge/tier-1 launch path on this dev host, and
+  # it IS tracked here — so the URL supply belongs in this line, not in
+  # tests/gate.sh. The gate deliberately refuses to self-default or probe for
+  # DUCKBRAIN_URL (AC4: a genuinely absent URL must still fail closed with exit
+  # 2 at the preflight); supplying it here keeps that refusal intact while
+  # giving the tier-1 launcher the local DuckBrain it needs. Changing the URL
+  # later is a one-line edit in this file, never a weakening of the gate.
+  test_command: DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000 bash tests/gate.sh
